WEBVTT

0
00:00.299 --> 00:01.203
<v Krista>In this video we're talking</v>

1
00:01.203 --> 00:03.265
about unit multipliers and unit multipliers

2
00:03.265 --> 00:04.619
basically just help us get from

3
00:04.619 --> 00:07.134
one set of units to another set of units.

4
00:07.134 --> 00:08.174
So, in this first problem,

5
00:08.174 --> 00:09.390
we've been asked to figure out

6
00:09.390 --> 00:12.592
how many yards there are in 360 inches.

7
00:12.592 --> 00:13.889
So, the first thing we need to realize

8
00:13.889 --> 00:15.572
is that we're starting with inches, right?

9
00:15.572 --> 00:17.860
We've been told we have 360 inches,

10
00:17.860 --> 00:21.553
so we're starting with inches and we need to get to yards.

11
00:21.553 --> 00:25.091
We don't know how many yards is equal to 360 inches,

12
00:25.091 --> 00:27.682
but we're starting at inches and we need to get to yards.

13
00:27.682 --> 00:30.523
Starting at inches, we have 360 of them.

14
00:30.523 --> 00:33.856
So, 360 inches. We want to get to yards,

15
00:34.700 --> 00:37.358
and your units tell you what you need to do.

16
00:37.358 --> 00:38.993
In order for us to get to yards

17
00:38.993 --> 00:41.986
and have an answer at the end that just says x, yards,

18
00:41.986 --> 00:45.149
however many yards we have that's equal to 360 inches,

19
00:45.149 --> 00:47.913
we're going to have to get rid of our inches units.

20
00:47.913 --> 00:49.655
Those are going to have to drop away eventually

21
00:49.655 --> 00:52.219
because we're going to need an answer that says x, yards.

22
00:52.219 --> 00:54.384
The only way to get rid of inches

23
00:54.384 --> 00:57.051
is to divide by the inches unit,

24
00:58.124 --> 01:00.232
so we know we are going to need inches in the denominator.

25
01:00.232 --> 01:02.606
You almost have to treat your units in the same way that

26
01:02.606 --> 01:04.542
you treat whole numbers or variables.

27
01:04.542 --> 01:08.508
In the same way that if we have 10x over 10,

28
01:08.508 --> 01:10.373
we know that we can cancel the 10

29
01:10.373 --> 01:13.323
in the numerator and the denominator, same thing here,

30
01:13.323 --> 01:14.658
when we have inches in the numerator

31
01:14.658 --> 01:16.055
and inches in the denominator,

32
01:16.055 --> 01:17.757
we know we're going to be able to cancel them.

33
01:17.757 --> 01:18.613
So this is the only way

34
01:18.613 --> 01:20.184
we're going to be able to get rid of them.

35
01:20.184 --> 01:22.640
But we're also going to need yards in our problem.

36
01:22.640 --> 01:24.588
And we're going to need yards to end up in the numerator

37
01:24.588 --> 01:26.987
in order to get an answer that's in terms of yards.

38
01:26.987 --> 01:30.403
So, we could put yards up here in the numerator,

39
01:30.403 --> 01:32.414
but then we'd have to use this fraction

40
01:32.414 --> 01:35.201
to describe the relationship between yards and inches,

41
01:35.201 --> 01:36.428
and we don't really know exactly

42
01:36.428 --> 01:38.631
how many inches are in a yard.

43
01:38.631 --> 01:41.210
However, we do know how many inches are in a foot,

44
01:41.210 --> 01:44.886
so instead of putting yards here, we can put feet

45
01:44.886 --> 01:48.613
and then we can say that there is one foot in 12 inches.

46
01:48.613 --> 01:49.983
What's going to happen when we do this,

47
01:49.983 --> 01:51.375
when we multiply these out,

48
01:51.375 --> 01:53.787
our inches are going to cancel,

49
01:53.787 --> 01:56.450
and you can see that the only units we have left are feet,

50
01:56.450 --> 01:57.995
which means our answer would be in feet

51
01:57.995 --> 01:59.274
if we did nothing else.

52
01:59.274 --> 02:01.327
But, remember, we need our answer in yards,

53
02:01.327 --> 02:05.278
so what we're going to have to do is multiply again.

54
02:05.278 --> 02:08.069
We're going to to at least have to put feet in the denominator

55
02:08.069 --> 02:10.528
so that we can get feet and feet to cancel.

56
02:10.528 --> 02:12.699
Now, we want to see if we can put yards

57
02:12.699 --> 02:15.992
in the numerator because we know we want yards

58
02:15.992 --> 02:17.171
in our final answer.

59
02:17.171 --> 02:20.318
So, now, do we know a relationship between feet and yards?

60
02:20.318 --> 02:22.548
Well, yeah, that's a relationship we should know.

61
02:22.548 --> 02:25.462
There's one yard for every three feet.

62
02:25.462 --> 02:28.068
Now, you can cancel feet in the numerator

63
02:28.068 --> 02:29.867
and feet in the denominator

64
02:29.867 --> 02:32.170
and you can see that all of our units are canceled,

65
02:32.170 --> 02:34.332
except for yards, and that's what we want.

66
02:34.332 --> 02:35.651
We wanted to get to yards.

67
02:35.651 --> 02:37.236
So, now that we're at this point,

68
02:37.236 --> 02:39.418
we just have to multiply across through the numerators

69
02:39.418 --> 02:41.510
and multiply across through the denominator

70
02:41.510 --> 02:43.809
and leave these units that we want leftover.

71
02:43.809 --> 02:47.192
So, 360 times one times one is 360,

72
02:47.192 --> 02:50.863
and in the denominator, 12 times three is 36.

73
02:50.863 --> 02:54.666
We have 36, and we're going to leave our yards units here.

74
02:54.666 --> 02:57.576
360 divided by 36 is equal to 10,

75
02:57.576 --> 03:01.326
so we get 10 yards as our final answer.

76
03:01.326 --> 03:05.261
Which means that there are 10 yards in 360 inches.

77
03:05.261 --> 03:06.710
Now, let's look at a second example.

78
03:06.710 --> 03:09.174
In this one, we want to figure out how many centimeters

79
03:09.174 --> 03:11.301
are in 1.4 kilometers.

80
03:11.301 --> 03:13.815
So, we're starting with kilometers

81
03:13.815 --> 03:16.475
and we need to get to centimeters.

82
03:16.475 --> 03:17.888
Okay, so starting with kilometers,

83
03:17.888 --> 03:19.535
how many kilometers do we have?

84
03:19.535 --> 03:21.195
We know that we have 1.4 kilometers,

85
03:21.195 --> 03:23.926
so we're going to put that over here on the left-hand side.

86
03:23.926 --> 03:25.855
Now, remember, our units immediately

87
03:25.855 --> 03:27.416
tell us what we need to do.

88
03:27.416 --> 03:28.510
We know eventually,

89
03:28.510 --> 03:30.125
we're going to have to get rid of kilometers,

90
03:30.125 --> 03:33.900
so we're going to need kilometers in our denominator

91
03:33.900 --> 03:34.733
no matter what.

92
03:34.733 --> 03:37.586
What do we know that has a relationship with kilometers?

93
03:37.586 --> 03:42.301
We know that there are 1000 meters in every one kilometer,

94
03:42.301 --> 03:43.816
so we can at least write that.

95
03:43.816 --> 03:45.771
Now we know that we'll be able to cancel our kilometers,

96
03:45.771 --> 03:47.796
but we're going to be left with meters,

97
03:47.796 --> 03:49.917
and we need to get from meters to centimeters.

98
03:49.917 --> 03:52.117
Remember centimeters is our final destination.

99
03:52.117 --> 03:53.864
So, do we have a relationship between

100
03:53.864 --> 03:55.303
centimeters and meters?

101
03:55.303 --> 03:56.491
Well, we do.

102
03:56.491 --> 03:59.120
We know that there are 100 centimeters in every meter.

103
03:59.120 --> 04:00.790
Again, with our unit multipliers,

104
04:00.790 --> 04:03.484
we know we're going to need meters in the denominator,

105
04:03.484 --> 04:06.638
because we need to cancel this meters with this one.

106
04:06.638 --> 04:09.865
And now we know that there are 100 centimeters

107
04:09.865 --> 04:11.595
in every one meter.

108
04:11.595 --> 04:13.230
Now, if we look at our units here,

109
04:13.230 --> 04:15.449
we're going to be able to cancel kilometers in the numerator

110
04:15.449 --> 04:16.911
and kilometers in the denominator,

111
04:16.911 --> 04:20.419
cancel meters in the numerator and meters in the denominator

112
04:20.419 --> 04:22.795
and the only units left are centimeters,

113
04:22.795 --> 04:23.899
which is perfect because we need

114
04:23.899 --> 04:25.802
our final answer in centimeters.

115
04:25.802 --> 04:27.168
So now that we're in that position,

116
04:27.168 --> 04:30.037
we just go ahead and multiply across our numerators.

117
04:30.037 --> 04:34.919
So we have 1.4 times 1000 times 100 is going to be 14

118
04:34.919 --> 04:38.876
with one, two, three, and then an extra two zeros.

119
04:38.876 --> 04:41.588
But then I'm going to move the decimal place over one,

120
04:41.588 --> 04:43.387
so this guy's going to go away,

121
04:43.387 --> 04:46.704
and I'm going to be left with one, two, three

122
04:46.704 --> 04:49.347
140,000 in the numerator.

123
04:49.347 --> 04:51.489
In the denominator, I have one times one,

124
04:51.489 --> 04:52.670
so I'll have one here.

125
04:52.670 --> 04:55.421
And then the only thing that's left is our centimeters,

126
04:55.421 --> 04:57.078
so I'm going to do centimeters.

127
04:57.078 --> 04:58.859
And now, if I just write this more cleanly,

128
04:58.859 --> 05:01.692
I'm going to have 140,000 centimeters

129
05:03.098 --> 05:07.181
are the number of centimeters in 1.4 kilometers.